---
import Details from "../../components/Details.astro";
import { siteInfo } from "../../constants/site-info";
import ProseLayout from "../../layouts/ProseLayout.astro";

const title = "About";
const description = "Pushing pixels (non-derogatory).";
---

<ProseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <strong>My name is Ky Decker.</strong>
  <Details id="design" summary="I design and build digital interfaces.">
    <Details
      id="web-design-systems"
      summary="Mostly for the web, and often involving design systems."
    >
      <p>
        I like making tidy work of messes. I like deleting code. I like making
        interfaces look great and function well. Working on design systems
        combines all of these in a way I find satisfying! I find inspiration
        from <a href="https://bell.bz">Andy Bell</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://ericwbailey.website">Eric Bailey</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://arielsalminen.com">Ariel Salminen</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://www.sarasoueidan.com">Sara Soueidan</a>,{" "}
        <a href="https://bradfrost.com">Brad Frost</a>, and{" "}
        <a href="https://aresluna.org">Marcin Wichary</a>, among many others
        (some of whom you can find via the <a href="/webrings">webrings</a> on
        this site).
      </p>
      <p>
        I occasionally <a href="/posts">write</a> about things I've built. Posts
        are available via <a href={siteInfo.socials.rss.href}>RSS</a>.
      </p>
    </Details>
    <Details id="career" summary="I've been doing this for over a decade.">
      <Details
        id="namesake"
        summary="I currently lead design and development at Namesake."
      >
        <p>
          <a href="https://namesake.fyi">Namesake</a> is a non-profit I
          co-founded to assist trans people in the US with legal name changes.
          We create{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/namesakefyi/namesake">
            open source tools
          </a>{" "}
          that have helped thousands of people update their legal name and
          gender marker.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm proud of the work we do at Namesake. If you have the capacity, you
          can{" "}
          <a href="https://namesake.fyi/donate">donate to support our work</a>.
        </p>
      </Details>
      <Details
        id="previous-jobs"
        summary="Before that, I worked at Scribe, Cityblock, and Dropbox, among others."
      >
        <p>
          I've worked under the title of "Product Designer", "UX Engineer", and
          more recently, "Design Engineer". Although the names and the tools
          have changed over time, the things I do have mostly remained constant:
          exploring a problem, evaluating solutions, and then working to build
          something (which, in turn, continues to inform the design of the
          solution). This is a long-winded way of saying I enjoy doing a little
          bit of everything.
        </p>
        <p>
          For my full work history, you can <a href="/resume">view my resume</a>
          . You can also read case studies about my{" "}
          <a href="/posts/data-driven">
            data-driven approach to design system management at Scribe
          </a>{" "}
          and{" "}
          <a href="/posts/commonplace">
            how I helped build Cityblock's design system
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </Details>
      <Details
        id="previous-jobs"
        summary="I started my career by designing themes for a Nintendo fan forum."
      >
        <p>
          I've been designing and coding for the web since around 2007, when my
          favorite website—NSider, Nintendo's official forum—shut down without
          warning.
        </p>
        <p>
          As members of NSider scattered to the winds, I joined a fan forum. I
          wanted the forum to look nicer, so I spent evenings after school
          designing assets in Photoshop and learning how to write CSS. I started
          by authoring CSS directly into a little textarea in the admin
          interface of{" "}
          <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/VBulletin">vBulletin</a>. No
          automatic formatting or syntax highlighting, and this was still before
          modern layout utilities like flexbox. It was tedious and I loved it.
        </p>
        <p>
          I owe my career to the fact that the web, unlike most other platforms,
          allows anyone to right click and "view source". The ability to peek
          under the hood and play around with styles felt like such a
          superpower. I still like writing CSS!
        </p>
      </Details>
    </Details>
  </Details>
  <Details id="location" summary="I live in New York City.">
    <Details
      id="hometown"
      summary="I've been in NYC since 2017. I'm originally from the South."
    >
      <p>
        I was born in Florida and grew up in North Carolina. I attended UNC
        Greensboro and have a Bachelor of Arts in Music with a minor in Computer
        Science.
      </p>
      <p>
        I now live in Ridgewood, Queens, with my partner, my cat, my piano, a
        handful of synthesizers, two dozen houseplants, my bike, and (proudly,
        since 2015) no car. (I'd like to live the rest of my life in places
        where I can bike, walk, and take a train wherever I need to go.)
      </p>
    </Details>
    <Details
      id="hobbies"
      summary="I like arranging music and taking photos of birds."
    >
      <p>
        I've published a few solo piano <a href="/arrangements">arrangements</a>{" "}
        that I created using LilyPond, a text-based music engraving language. To
        get away from screens, I like looking at birds. I share my photography
        on <a href="https://glass.photo/kydecker">Glass</a>.
      </p>
    </Details>
  </Details>
  <Details id="contact" summary="I'm online; say hello.">
    <p>
      You can find me on <a href={siteInfo.socials.arena.href}>Are.na</a>,{" "}
      <a href={siteInfo.socials.github.href}>GitHub</a>, and{" "}
      <small>(shudder)</small>{" "}
      <a href={siteInfo.socials.linkedin.href}>LinkedIn</a>. You can email me at{" "}
      <a href="mailto:hi@ky.fyi">hi@ky.fyi</a>—I may not reply immediately, but
      my inbox is always open. Thanks for visiting and clicking in. Don't forget
      to sign the <a href="/guestbook">guestbook</a> before you go.
    </p>
  </Details>
</ProseLayout>
